# Dependency refresh

Status: implementation and hosted candidate builds complete; installed acceptance
pending. Work is in `dependency-refresh`, based on main
`b3d3235c78e513c3202b9524f1fea8ae420787bd`. No release or installation is
authorized by this plan. SDL remains an active dependency.

## Scope and order

1. Remove unused x265 encoder/build/link/patch inputs. Retain x264, NVENC,
   VideoToolbox, HEVC decoding and the existing encoded decoder test vectors.
2. Upgrade Quinn 0.11.12 / quinn-proto 0.11.19 / quinn-udp 0.5.16,
   Rustls 0.23.46, webpki 0.103.16 and Tokio 1.54.1. Production and probe
   lockfiles must resolve the same transport versions. Retire local fixes only
   when upstream behavior and regression tests prove equivalence.
3. Reconcile Kyber 0.29.0 with the maintained Kymux/Kyproto fork. Keep RaptorQ
   2.0.1, `plank-native/2`, bounded parsers/queues, cancellation, completed-FEC
   draining, telemetry, fixed-MTU policy and the accepted rate controller.
   Do not restore application datagram pacing or upstream RaptorQ 1.x.
4. Upgrade FFmpeg to 9.0.2 on Linux Host and desktop Clients; SDL to 3.4.18;
   Mac bundled Opus to 1.6.1, OpenSSL to 3.5.9 LTS and FreeType to 2.15.0.
   Preserve exact identity-GBR decoding and independently verified patches.
5. Evaluate Boost 1.92.0, Rust 1.99.1, paired Vulkan 1.4.367 and JSON 3.12.0
   as separate commits/checkpoints. Preserve the Vulkan allocation-failure
   repair and negative-control regression coverage.
6. Qt 6.12 and the Intel media stack require separate packaging/hardware
   qualification. Ubuntu currently uses distribution Qt 6.10.2 and VA-API;
   adding oneVPL/QSV is not a dependency refresh. Do not replace system graphics
   or audio packages incidentally. Native Apple/AVP inputs are a separate
   integration and must receive relevant security/media fixes without merging
   unfinished product features into main.

## Fixed contracts

- NVIDIA 595.104.02, CUDA 13.2 Update 2, NVENC SDK 13.0 remain; SDK 13.1
  requires a newer driver outside the approved baseline.
- macOS Client 15+ and Host 26.7+, built with SDK 27+; Rocky 9.7 / Ubuntu 26.04.
- No codec/chroma/precision/range substitutions or transport wire downgrade.
- Keep all required dependency patches reproducible and fail closed on drift.
- Build candidates on GitHub-hosted Actions with exact pins and provenance.
  Do not publish a release, merge, deploy or claim hardware acceptance.

## Validation

Run focused source/component tests for each stage, then clean-bootstrap hosted
packages for all affected products. Verify package dependency closure, source
hashes, platform floors, cache fingerprints and branch-qualified versions.
Transport gates cover queue/MTU bounds, malformed traffic, cancellation,
reconnect and intentional loss. Media gates cover exact 8/10-bit identity,
hardware/software decoding and presentation, 4K/5K and two-display canvases.
Actual hardware sessions, listening/A/V soak, Wacom recovery and macOS 15/26.7/27
acceptance remain explicit installed-package gates, not compiler results.

Record stage commits, upstream provenance, replaced/retained patches, results
and remaining gates in HANDOFF; retain final packages in the versioned catalog.

## Qualification checkpoint — 2026-11-01

All four desktop candidates are built and collected as `1.2.14-dependency-refresh`
(the Mac Host also carries its 26.7 floor). Both Mac PKGs are signed/notarized.
Both Clients and the Mac Host use root `1765331`; the Linux Host uses `f53cdc9`
with the later Vulkan update and corrected Boost test pin. HANDOFF records full commits,
package hashes, runs and pending hardware gates. Both native transport send
paths passed three 150 Mbps loss matrices each; all 5,400 frames were recovered.
Vulkan's 52 targeted cases and intentional-failure negative control passed.
No candidate has been installed, merged or released. Keep Qt/Intel/oneVPL and
native Apple/AVP work separate from this qualified dependency checkpoint.
